<time datetime="2023-05-22">May 22, 2023</time>
<article id="JavaScript" class="WebBits">
    <h2>TRY: Disabling JavaScript</h2>
    <p>
        JavaScript dominates the web for being the most common underlying code
        to make a website interactive. Useful for buttons, panels, and
        component interactions, <abbr title="JavaScript">JS</abbr> is loaded
        with a page along with
        <abbr title="HyperText Markup Language">HTML</abbr> and
        <abbr title="Cascading Style Sheet">CSS</abbr>.
    </p>
    <p>
        A website may break without JavaScript functions. This can be
        simulated in the <abbr title="developer">dev</abbr> tools, as such:
    </p>
    <details open>
        <summary>Firefox</summary>
        <ol>
            <li>
                Open Firefox preferences by typing
                <span class="url">about:config</span> in the address bar
            </li>
            <li>Search "JavaScript"</li>
            <li>Toggle 'javascript.enabled' to false</li>
            <li>Refresh the page</li>
        </ol>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Chrome and Edge</summary>
        <ol>
            <li>Open Dev tools: <kbd><kbd>CTRL</kbd>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<kbd>SHIFT</kbd>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<kbd>J</kbd></kbd></li>
            <li>
                Run command "JavaScript":
                <kbd><kbd>CTRL</kbd>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<kbd>SHIFT</kbd>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<kbd>P</kbd></kbd>
            </li>
            <li>Click "Disable"</li>
            <li>Refresh the page</li>
        </ol>
    </details>
    <p>
        Different websites may portray its disablement differently.
        <span data-rwb-type="link">
            <a href="https://www.randomwebbits.com/" target="_blank"
               title="&lt;RWB&gt;">Random Web Bits'</a>
        </span>
        header/footer will not show up. Navigation is only available if you
        know the relative <abbr title="Uniform Resource Locator">URL</abbr> or
        utilize the back/forward buttons.
    </p>
</article>
<acronyms-list></acronyms-list>
<div class="Top-Link"><a class="Top" href="/pages/javascript#top">Top</a></div>
